[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086025584","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121804#issuecomment-5086025584","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121804","id":5086025584,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLyaXcA","user":{"login":"Kyzzsa","id":53786793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzg2Nzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53786793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa","html_url":"https://github.com/Kyzzsa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T00:02:02Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T00:02:02Z","body":"The reason dragging the slider far to the left can produce smaller values is that the slider's underlying input provides a **negative ratio**. \n\nThe remaining issue stems from Godot's range calculation method, where `0` is effectively being treated as `1`. It interpolates the logarithm of the value directly using the ratio, with code equivalent to:\n\n```plaintext\nexp_min = log2(min_val)\nexp_max = log2(max_val)\nexp_val = lerp(exp_min, exp_max, ratio)\nvalue = exp2(exp_val)\n```\n\nThis necessitates that `min_val` be strictly greater than `0`, since `log2(0)` is undefined. In practice, the implementation falls back to:\n\n```plaintext\nexp_min = min_val == 0 ? 0 : log2(min_val)\n```\n\nAs a result, a `min_val` of `0` is effectively treated as `exp2(0)`, which equals `1` — and this is precisely what introduces the discontinuity described in this issue.\n\nIf we shift the interval `[min_val, max_val]` to `[1, 1 + max_val - min_val]`, the logic becomes:\n\n```plaintext\nexp_max = log2(1 + max_val - min_val)\nvalue = exp2(exp_max * ratio) + min_val - 1\n```\n\nThis resolves the problem entirely. Furthermore, `min_val` can now be **any valid floating-point number**, rather than being restricted to non-negative values.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086025584/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086040538","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121804#issuecomment-5086040538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121804","id":5086040538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLybR2g","user":{"login":"Kyzzsa","id":53786793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzg2Nzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53786793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa","html_url":"https://github.com/Kyzzsa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T00:05:45Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T00:17:04Z","body":"If you are not working on this, I will open a PR to address it. 😉","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086040538/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086432091","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121804#issuecomment-5086432091","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121804","id":5086432091,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLyzLWw","user":{"login":"Kyzzsa","id":53786793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzg2Nzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53786793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa","html_url":"https://github.com/Kyzzsa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T01:33:25Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T08:54:59Z","body":"I just realized that changing the logic of exponential scaling would be somewhat breaking. Even setting that aside, there are still inherent issues with the approach.\n\nIf we adopt the solution shifting the interval to `[start, start + max_val - min_val]` before taking the logarithm—the choice of `start` significantly affects the interpolation result. For example, with `start = 1`, values in a small range like `[0, 0.1]` would produce results that are almost linear rather than exponential. Or perhaps we could export this offset property?\n\nA compromise would be to assign a tiny value to `0` in the original method:\n\n```\nexp_min = min_val == 0 ? -6 * log2(10) : log2(min_val)   // equivalent to min_val = 1e-6\n```\n\nAlternatively, we could simply disallow the use of `0` explicitly.\n\nSo in summary, we have three options:\n1. Shift the interval to `[start, start + max_val - min_val]` and then take the logarithm.\n2. Add a small epsilon so that `0` behaves like `1e-6` instead of `1`.\n3. Drop support for `min_val = 0`.\n\nMaybe I should open an issue to consult the maintainers' opinions? I think they're likely to go with option 2.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086432091/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086680769","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121804#issuecomment-5086680769","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121804","id":5086680769,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABLzCWwQ","user":{"login":"Kyzzsa","id":53786793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzg2Nzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53786793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa","html_url":"https://github.com/Kyzzsa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T02:26:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T02:27:31Z","body":"I will open a PR for option 2, since it does not affect the behaviour except when `min_val = 0`.\n\nHowever `1E-6` is too small comparing to an average exponential interpolation, and would make it overly skewed towards the end. Moreover, it may produce values displayed as zero despite being non-zero in an `EditorSpinSlider`, which could lead to unintended input. To avoid that, I will use `1E-3`, which is the default step of a `EditorSpinSlider`.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5086680769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5088201531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121804#issuecomment-5088201531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121804","id":5088201531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABL0fLOw","user":{"login":"Kyzzsa","id":53786793,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzg2Nzkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53786793?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa","html_url":"https://github.com/Kyzzsa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kyzzsa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-27T06:53:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-27T20:33:09Z","body":"The final solution is a combination of option 1 and 2. Only when `exp_min` is zero will the interval be shifted to `[epsilon, epsilon + max_val - min_val]`","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5088201531/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]